/Alt (Flowchart illustrating EEG signal processing. EEG signals enter datasets \(MAT, STEW\) and undergo segmentation. A ten-level decomposition via EMFD enables entropy-based feature extraction. Two paths for classification: 7 machine learning classifiers and 5 optimized classifiers, both assessed by performance metrics. Task and rest states indicated.)
/K [1237 0 R 1238 0 R 1239 0 R 1240 0 R 1241 0 R 1242 0 R 1243 0 R]
/P 40 0 R
/S /Figure
/T <FEFF004600690067007500720065>
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
193 0 obj
<<
/Alt (Line graph comparing rest and task signals. The x-axis represents samples from zero to two thousand, and the y-axis shows amplitude in microvolts from negative forty to forty. The pink line indicates rest, and the blue line indicates task, with visible fluctuations in amplitude for both.)
/K [1244 0 R 1245 0 R 1246 0 R 1247 0 R 1248 0 R 1249 0 R 1250 0 R]
/P 40 0 R
/S /Figure
